# .claude/state/chain-sessions-green/ — chain-spawned session artifacts that
# passed /chain_audit with verdict GREEN and received explicit user approval
# during the interactive audit.
#
# Sibling of:
#   .claude/state/chain-sessions/     — LIVE queue of un-audited headless runs
#   .claude/state/chain-archive/      — frozen chain.json snapshots from /chain reset
#
# On GREEN + approval, /chain_audit moves:
#   - .claude/state/chain-sessions/<plan>.log
#   - .claude/state/chain-sessions/<plan>.pid
#   - ~/.claude/projects/c--Users-rutvi-projects-encore-framework/<uuid>.jsonl
#     (the claude -p transcript that references <plan>)
# INTO this folder. Filenames are preserved; the uuid transcript is renamed
# to include the plan name for self-identification.
#
# YELLOW/RED audits do NOT move anything — artifacts stay in chain-sessions/
# until the user fixes and re-audits to GREEN.
#
# NOTHING else (manual cleanup, /chain reset, agent tidy-up) may touch
# chain-sessions/*.log. See LR-042.
#
# claude --resume <uuid> will NOT work on transcripts moved here — the desktop
# app and --resume index only look at ~/.claude/projects/. That's intentional:
# moved = "audited GREEN, no longer needs interactive replay."
